e Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports ON-CAMPUS SERVICES Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Employment Opportunities Luminary Fellow – Accounting Co-op & MSA Back to Employment Opportunities Luminary Fellow – Accounting Co-op & MSA Posted: September 11, 2026 Position Code: 72 Position Summary The Luminary Fellow for Accounting Co-op and MSA oversees the accounting co-op experience and supports the evolution of the graduate accounting program toward an advisory- and consulting-focused model. This role serves as a bridge between students, employers, and the school, ensuring a high-quality, career-aligned experience. Key Responsibilities Co-op Program Leadership Oversee all aspects of the accounting co-op program, including: ○ student preparation ○ placement coordination ○ employer engagement Maintain relationships with accounting firms and industry partners Ensure alignment between co-op experiences and student learning goals Student Mentorship & Career Development Provide guidance on: ○ resume and cover letter development ○ interview preparation ○ professional readiness Mentor students throughout the co-op process and during placements Employer & Partner Engagement Serve as primary liaison with accounting firms and partner organizations Coordinate communication and feedback between students and employers Identify and develop new co-op opportunities Instruction & Course Delivery Teach and manage the accounting co-op course Integrate structured reflection and learning into the co-op experience Evaluate student performance and provide feedback Program Development (Graduate Accounting) Advise on the evolution of the graduate accounting program toward: ○ advisory ○ consulting ○ decision-support skills Provide practitioner insight into curriculum design and program positioning Qualifications Significant professional experience in accounting, audit, advisory, or consulting Strong understanding of career pathways within accounting and related fields Experience mentoring or developing early-career professionals Excellent communication and organizational skills Preferred Experience working with accounting firms (public or advisory) Teaching or training experience Exposure to advisory, consulting, or client-facing roles Position Type Part-time (Luminary Fellow) Combination of program management, mentorship, and instruction Application Materials Should Include: Resume Cover letter stating motivation and interest in the position, citing experience relevant to the qualifications and including experience with, and commitment to, our Catholic Augustinian mission and our values. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,100 undergraduate, 2,500 graduate students and 50 doctoral students from 48 states and 63 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business and the graduate school of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 38th in the Regional Universities North category in 2026. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Salary Range: $55000.00 - $60000.00 Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Visual & Performing Arts Merrimack College Marching Marching Band’s Fall 2024 Exciting Events The Merrimack College Band had a very exciting Fall semester, including their first international trip. Request More Info Visit Our Campus Apply Now! Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions I