      "description": "Assistant Professor of Practice (Non-Tenure Track) – Economics | Merrimack College Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid Student Accounts Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus Housing & Residence Life Dining Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education Student Involvement Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-Campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Apply Visit See Programs Employment Opportunities Assistant Professor of Practice (Non-Tenure Track) – Economics Back to Employment Opportunities Assistant Professor of Practice (Non-Tenure Track) – Economics Posted: October 8, 2026 Position Code: 2095 Position Overview: The Girard School of Business at Merrimack College invites applications for a full-time, 9-month, non-tenure track assistant professor of practice position in Economics beginning in Fall 2027. Rank will be commensurate with the successful candidate’s academic accomplishments, teaching experience, and qualifications. The Girard School is seeking an outstanding educator to play a central role in the continued development of Merrimack College’s new B.S. in Economics. This is a teaching-focused position for a faculty member who is passionate about making economics rigorous, relevant, and accessible to undergraduate students and who is excited by the opportunity to help build a new academic program. Responsibilities Teach undergraduate Economics courses across the curriculum consistent with program needs and the candidate’s expertise; Deliver engaging, rigorous, and student-centered instruction to students with varied levels of prior exposure to economics and quantitative methods; Contribute to the continued development and refinement of the B.S. in Economics curriculum. Advise and mentor Economics students and support their academic and professional development; Participate in assessment and other activities necessary to support the quality and growth of the Economics program; Collaborate with Economics and Girard School faculty on curricular and programmatic initiatives; Contribute to the service and intellectual life of the Girard School and Merrimack College. Qualifications We seek an economist who is first and foremost an excellent teacher—someone capable of introducing students to economic thinking while also challenging more advanced students to apply economic theory and empirical methods to consequential real-world questions. The successful candidate should be comfortable teaching across multiple areas of the undergraduate Economics curriculum. Areas of teaching expertise may include: principles of microeconomics and macroeconomics; intermediate microeconomic and macroeconomic theory; econometrics and applied economic analysis; money, banking, and financial markets; labor economics; public economics and public policy; international economics; economics of technology and innovation; and other applied fields consistent with the needs of the program. We particularly value faculty who can connect economic concepts to questions students encounter in the world around them and help students develop the analytical, quantitative, and critical-thinking skills associated with the discipline. Required Qualifications Ph.D. in Economics or a closely related field. Demonstrated ability or strong potential to teach Economics effectively at the undergraduate level, particularly through familiarity with the use and application of AI in the field of Economics and the ability to assess student learning outcomes in an AI-enabled environment. Ability to teach across multiple areas of the undergraduate Economics curriculum. Commitment to student learning, mentorship, and inclusive teaching practices. Preferred Qualifications A record of excellence in undergraduate teaching. Experience teaching introductory and intermediate Economics courses. Ability to teach econometrics, applied economics, or other quantitatively oriented courses. Experience contributing to curriculum or program development. Evidence of success mentoring and advising undergraduate students. Application Materials Should Include: Curriculum vitae Cover letter stating motivation and interest in the position, citing experience relevant to the qualifications and experience associated with key responsibilities for the position including teaching philosophy and evaluations. Contact information for three professional references (name, title, address, phone number, email address). References will be contacted only at a later stage of the search process. Compensation The expected 9-month base salary range (paid over 12 months) for the Assistant Professor of Practice rank is $80,000-$105,000. The actual pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as, but not limited to, candidate qualifications and prior experience, scope of responsibilities, internal equity, and market considerations. Work Location This is an on-campus position as employees are essential in order to provide a fully on-campus, residential college experience for our students and the community. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,100 undergraduate, 2,500 graduate students and 50 doctoral students from 48 states and 63 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business and the graduate school of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 38th in the Regional Universities North category in 2026. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Salary Range: $80,000 - $105,000 Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Request More Info Visit Campus Apply Now Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Can