      "title": "Open Rank Professor of Accounting (Non-Tenure Track)",
      "description": "Open Rank Professor of Accounting (Non-Tenure Track) — Analytics, Technology & Advisory | Merrimack College Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid Student Accounts Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus Housing & Residence Life Dining Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education Student Involvement Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-Campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Apply Visit See Programs Employment Opportunities Open Rank Professor of Accounting (Non-Tenure Track) — Analytics, Technology & Advisory Back to Employment Opportunities Open Rank Professor of Accounting (Non-Tenure Track) — Analytics, Technology & Advisory Posted: October 8, 2026 Position Code: 3005 Position Overview: The Girard School of Business at Merrimack College invites applications for a full-time, open-rank faculty position in Accounting beginning in Fall 2027. The Girard School is seeking a faculty member who can help shape the future of accounting education and applied scholarship as artificial intelligence, analytics, automation, and evolving professional practices change both the work accountants perform and the value they provide to organizations. We are particularly interested in candidates who combine meaningful professional or industry experience with a strong commitment to teaching, scholarship, and external engagement. This position is part of a broader strategic investment in faculty, academic programs, research, experiential learning, and industry engagement within the Girard School. The successful candidate will have a significant opportunity to help shape the continued evolution and differentiation of the School’s M.S. in Accounting, while contributing to undergraduate Accounting education and the School’s growing network of experiential and industry partnerships. The Girard School believes the next generation of accounting education must extend beyond technical preparation alone. As technology assumes a greater role in routine accounting, analysis, and compliance activities—and as pathways to CPA licensure continue to evolve—graduate accounting education has an opportunity to prepare professionals for increasingly important roles in advisory services, analytics, risk, technology, strategic decision support, and organizational leadership. The successful candidate will help Merrimack explore and develop this next generation of accounting education while maintaining the strong technical foundation essential to the profession. Responsibilities Teach undergraduate and graduate Accounting courses consistent with the candidate’s expertise and the needs of the Girard School; Play a meaningful role in the continued development and differentiation of the M.S. in Accounting, including opportunities to expand graduate education in advisory services, analytics, artificial intelligence, technology, risk, and strategic decision support; Help ensure that Accounting curricula remain responsive to changes in professional practice, technology, employer needs, and pathways into the profession; Maintain an active program of applied scholarship and thought leadership focused on consequential problems facing organizations and industries. Relevant outputs may include applied research, white papers, industry reports, case studies, conference presentations, practitioner publications, and other scholarly or professional work that advances knowledge and informs practice; Develop and sustain relationships with accounting firms, corporate accounting and finance functions, advisory organizations, and other external partners that can support research, experiential learning, cooperative education, and student engagement; Translate challenges emerging from professional practice into opportunities for faculty research, student projects, cases, simulations, and other forms of applied learning; Mentor undergraduate and graduate students and engage students meaningfully in research and applied projects; Contribute to the intellectual life, service, and strategic development of the Girard School and Merrimack College; Where appropriate to the candidate’s scholarly and professional interests, contribute to the developing Center for the Future of Work and related Applied Industry Labs. Qualifications We are especially interested in candidates who are comfortable operating across academic and professional environments—individuals who understand the changing accounting profession, can identify important questions emerging from practice, study those questions rigorously, and translate their expertise into relevant teaching and student experiences. The Girard School welcomes candidates whose careers have crossed traditional boundaries between industry and academia, including accomplished accounting professionals, executives, consultants, and senior practitioners who have developed or are developing a substantive scholarly and teaching agenda. Relevant areas of scholarly and professional interest may include, but are not limited to: accounting analytics and data-driven decision-making; artificial intelligence and automation in accounting; advisory and consulting services; accounting technology and digital transformation; strategic decision support; risk management and internal controls; assurance and emerging forms of assurance; technology governance and responsible use of AI; financial analysis and organizational performance; the changing role and skills of accounting professionals; and taxation, particularly where it intersects with technology, analytics, advisory services, or organizational decision-making. Required Qualifications A doctorate or appropriate terminal degree in Accounting, Business Administration, or a closely related field by the time of appointment. Demonstrated ability or strong potential to teach effectively at the undergraduate and graduate levels. Evidence of an active or emerging scholarly agenda, appropriate to the candidate’s career stage, with interest in producing applied scholarship that addresses consequential organizational, market, or industry challenges. Demonstrated interest in engaging professional organizations and translating real-world challenges into scholarship and/or student learning. Preferred Qualifications Significant professional experience in public accounting, advisory or consulting services, corporate accounting, controllership, accounting technology, risk, assurance, taxation, or related areas. Experience applying analytics, artificial intelligence, automation, or emerging technologies to accounting and organizational problems. Experience in advisory, consulting, or other roles requiring accountants to translate financial and nonfinancial information into organizational decisions. Experience contributing to the development, redesign, or delivery of graduate or professional education. CPA or other relevant professional certification. A record of applied research, thought leadership, professional presentations, or other work that bridges scholarship and practice. Experience developing relationships across professional practice, industry, and academia. Interest in building new programs, research initiatives, partnerships, or experiential-learning models. Application Materials Should Include: Curriculum vitae Cover letter stating motivation and interest in the position, citing experience relevant to the qualifications and experience associated with key responsibilities for the position including teaching philosophy and evaluations. Contact information for three professional references (name, title, address, phone number, email address). References will be contacted only at a later stage of the search process. Compensation The expected 9-month base salary range for the Assistant Professor or Assistant Professor of Practice rank is $100,000-$125,000; for the Associate Professor or Associate Professor of Practice $125,000,000-$140,000; for the Professor or Professor of Practice $140,000-$160,000. The actual pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as, but not limited to, candidate qualifications and prior experience, scope of responsibilities, internal equity, and market considerations. Work Location This is an on-campus position as employees are essential in order to provide a fully on-campus, residential college experience for our students and the community. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,100 undergraduate, 2,500 graduate students and 50 doctoral students from 48 states and 63 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business and the graduate school of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 38th in the Regional Universities North category in 2026. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Salary Range: $80,000 - $160,000 Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Request More Info Visit Campus Apply Now Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info Maintenance Requests MyMack Web Editor Login Find People & Places Contact Us Employee Directory Faculty Directory Map and Directions Quick Links Athletics Bookstore Consumer Information Employment Events Calendar Give Library Offices and Services Parking and Transportation Terms of Use Title IX Together We Rise Copyright © 2026 Merrimack College. All Rights Reserved. Search Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Admission Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid Student Accounts Student Life Student Life Our Campus Housing & Residence Life Dining Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education Student Involvement Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About About Our Story & Happenings About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Service