      "description": "Director of Enrollment Operations | Merrimack College Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid Student Accounts Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus Housing & Residence Life Dining Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education Student Involvement Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-Campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Apply Visit See Programs Employment Opportunities Director of Enrollment Operations Back to Employment Opportunities Director of Enrollment Operations Posted: September 17, 2026 Position Code: 227 Position Overview: The Director of Enrollment Operations provides strategic and operational leadership for the systems, processes, and services that support undergraduate admission and new student matriculation. Reporting to the Dean of Undergraduate Admission, the Director oversees two Enrollment Operations Specialists and is responsible for advancing operational excellence, strengthening customer service, ensuring data integrity, and leveraging technology and automation to create efficient and scalable enrollment processes. The Director serves as a key operational partner to the Senior Director of Undergraduate Admission and Director of Transfer Admission, working closely with both leaders to translate recruitment and admission priorities into effective processes, workflows, and technology solutions. The Director also collaborates extensively with other campus partners, including Central Analytics, Athletics, and Student Life to ensure the accurate and timely exchange of information and a coordinated experience for students throughout the admission and matriculation process. The Director serves as a functional leader for our CRM system (Slate) and related enrollment technologies, using these systems to improve workflows, automate processes, reduce manual work, maintain data quality, and enhance service to students and families. The Director will also lead the practical application and adoption of artificial intelligence within Undergraduate Admission, developing AI-enabled workflows and tools, partnering with consultants and technical resources on more complex solutions, and building AI fluency across the undergraduate admission team. The Director also provides operational leadership and coordination for the matriculation of new first-year and transfer students, including onboarding tasks, completion tracking, student follow-up, and coordination with campus offices. Key areas of oversight and responsibility include: Enrollment Operations & Continuous Improvement Lead the day-to-day work and continued advancement of undergraduate enrollment operations, establishing effective processes, service standards, workflows, and quality-control practices. Evaluate existing processes and identify opportunities to simplify, standardize, automate, and scale operations while improving service to students and families. Develop and maintain clear documentation of operational processes, procedures, roles, and timelines. Anticipate operational needs throughout the enrollment cycle and ensure the team is prepared to respond effectively to changing volume, priorities, and deadlines. Establish and monitor measures of operational effectiveness, including accuracy, turnaround time, service levels, and completion rates. Identify operational challenges and recommend solutions that balance student experience, staff capacity, institutional priorities, and scalability. Enrollment Systems, Automation & Data Serve as a functional leader for Slate and other technologies supporting undergraduate admission and enrollment operations. Manage and optimize Slate functionality supporting operational processes, including workflows, rules, queries, forms, portals/checklists, communications, imports/exports, and related functionality. Lead the implementation and adoption of AI-enabled workflows and tools within Undergraduate Admission, including the development of AI agents and other solutions that improve operational efficiency, scalability, and service. Identify practical, high-value opportunities to incorporate AI into existing business processes and workflows. Partner with consultants and technical resources on the development of more complex AI solutions, helping define operational requirements, supporting development and testing, and ensuring solutions can be effectively integrated into the work of the team. Build AI fluency and adoption across Undergraduate Admission by providing guidance, training, tools, and practical use cases that help staff appropriately incorporate AI into their work. Represent Undergraduate Admission on the College’s AI Taskforce, collaborating with institutional partners and bringing relevant practices, tools, and opportunities back to the undergraduate admission team. Identify and implement opportunities to automate repetitive or manual processes, improve workflows, and build scalable solutions that increase operational capacity. Ensure the accuracy, consistency, and integrity of enrollment data through regular audits, testing, reconciliation, and quality-control practices. Work closely with the Office of Central Analytics and other campus partners on the exchange of information between Slate and institutional systems. Oversee the operational use of third-party enrollment platforms, including CollegeVine, Edvisorly, enrollML, Scoir, and other current or future technologies. Evaluate system functionality and emerging technologies and recommend enhancements that improve efficiency, scalability, data quality, or the student experience. Customer Service & Matriculation Lead customer-service operations for students and families across telephone, email, text, and other service channels, establishing expectations for timely, accurate, consistent, and student-centered support. Use service trends, student questions, and operational data to identify opportunities to improve processes, communications, and resources. Provide operational leadership and coordination for the matriculation of newly enrolling first-year and transfer students. Manage the operational infrastructure for new student onboarding in Slate, including tasks, checklists, forms, communications, and completion tracking. Coordinate with campus partners to ensure they receive timely and accurate information needed to support incoming students and that Admission receives the information necessary to monitor student progress. Monitor completion of required onboarding activities and coordinate proactive follow-up with students who have outstanding requirements, such as health forms, student ID photos, placement activities, and other required tasks. Identify gaps, bottlenecks, and points of confusion in the matriculation process and work with campus partners to improve the experience for students and families. Leadership & Collaboration Supervise, develop, and provide direction to two Enrollment Operations Specialists, establishing clear responsibilities, priorities, performance expectations, and opportunities for professional growth. Serve as a key operational partner to the Senior Director of Undergraduate Admission and Director of Transfer Admission, maintaining close communication around priorities, upcoming initiatives, operational needs, and challenges. Work collaboratively with admission leadership to develop operational approaches that effectively support first-year and transfer recruitment and admission strategies. Build strong working relationships with campus partners involved in the admission, enrollment, and onboarding of new students. Serve as an operational resource to campus partners, facilitating communication, problem-solving, and coordination when processes or responsibilities cross organizational areas. Foster a culture of continuous improvement, accountability, collaboration, and exceptional service within Enrollment Operations. Primary Responsibilities: Provide leadership for the processes and services that support undergraduate admission and new student matriculation. Continually assess operations and implement improvements that increase efficiency, accuracy, scalability, and service to students and families. Establish effective workflows, service standards, quality-control practices, documentation, and operational measures. Serve as a functional leader for Technolutions Slate and related enrollment technologies, identifying and implementing opportunities to streamline and automate processes, reduce manual work, improve workflows, and create scalable solutions that increase operational capacity. Lead the implementation and adoption of AI-enabled workflows and tools within Undergraduate Admission, including the development of AI agents and other solutions that improve operational efficiency and service. Partner with consultants and other technical resources on the development of more complex AI solutions, serving as the key Undergraduate Admission partner to ensure solutions address operational needs and can be effectively integrated into the work of the team. Establish and maintain processes to ensure enrollment data is accurate, consistent, timely, and reliable. Conduct and oversee audits, testing, reconciliation, and quality-control activities; identify and resolve data issues; and work closely with the Office of Central Analytics and campus partners on integrations, data standards, reporting needs, and the exchange of information between Slate and institutional systems. Lead the operational processes supporting the matriculation of newly enrolling first-year and transfer students. Manage onboarding tasks, checklists, forms, communications, and completion tracking in Slate; coordinate with campus partners to ensure timely and accurate exchange of student information; monitor completion of required activities; and coordinate proactive follow-up with students who have outstanding requirements. Oversee customer service to students and families across telephone, email, text, and other service channels. Establish expectations for timely, accurate, consistent, and student-centered service, and use inquiry trends and operational data to identify opportunities to improve processes, communications, resources, and the overall student experience. Develop and maintain highly collaborative working relationships with the Senior Director of Undergraduate Admission and Director of Transfer Admission. Work closely with both leaders to understand recruitment and admission priorities, anticipate operational needs, and translate priorities into effective processes, workflows, systems, and service strategies. Collaboratively identify and address operational challenges and opportunities affecting first-year and transfer admission. Supervise two Enrollment Operations Specialists, establishing clear responsibilities, priorities, performance expectations, and service standards. Provide coaching, training, professional development, and cross-training while fostering a culture of accountability, collaboration, continuous improvement, and exceptional service. Oversee the operational use of CollegeVine, Edvisorly, enrollML, Scoir, and other current or future enrollment technologies. Coordinate with vendors and internal partners to ensure effective implementation, integration, data exchange, troubleshooting, and use of these platforms. Evaluate emerging technologies and recommend solutions that improve efficiency, scalability, service, or operational effectiveness. Work collaboratively with campus offices involved in admission, enrollment, and new student onboarding. Facilitate effective communication, coordination, and problem-solving across organizational areas and ensure campus partners have timely, accurate information necessary to support incoming students. Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s Degree required, Masters preferred Knowledge, Skills, Abilities Strong understanding of operational processes, workflow design, automation, and continuous improvement. Strong working knowledge of CRM and related technology; knowledge of Technolutions Slate strongly preferred. Strong analytical and problem-solving skills with a commitment to data accuracy and integrity. Ability to translate business needs into effective, efficient, and scalable processes and technology solutions. Strong organizational and project management skills with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines. Excellent communication and interpersonal skills with the ability to build collaborative working relationships across functional areas. Strong commitment to high-quality customer service and the student experience. Experience 7-10 years of progressively responsible experience in operations, process improvement, systems/CRM administration, customer service operations, or a related area. Demonstrated experience improving operational processes through technology, workflow design, and automation. Supervisory or team leadership experience required. Experience in higher education, enrollment management, admission, or student services preferred, but not required. Application Materials Should Include: Resume or CV Cover letter stating motivation and interest in the position, citing experience relevant to the qualifications and including experience with, and commitment to, our Catholic Augustinian mission and our values. Work Location This is an on-campus position as employees are essential in order to provide a fully on-campus, residential college experience for our students and the community. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,100 undergraduate, 2,500 graduate students and 50 doctoral students from 48 states and 63 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business and the graduate school of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 38th in the Regional Universities North category in 2026. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Salary Range: $90,000 - $100,000 Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Request More Info Visit Campus Apply Now Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info Maintenance Requests MyMack Web Editor Login Find People & Places Contact Us Employee Directory Faculty Directory Map and Directions Quick Links Athletics Bookstore Consumer Information Employment Events Calendar Give Library Offices and Services Parking and Transportation Terms of Use Title IX Together We Rise Copyright © 2026 Merrimack College. All Rights Reserved. Search Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Admission Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fello