tics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-Campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Apply Visit See Programs Employment Opportunities Financial Aid Operations Specialist Back to Employment Opportunities Financial Aid Operations Specialist Posted: September 11, 2026 Position Code: 631 Position Overview The Financial Aid Operations Specialist coordinates a variety of interrelated operational, administrative, and customer service processes to support the timely and accurate delivery of financial aid. Reporting to the Director of Financial Aid, this position assists in maintaining compliance with federal, state, and institutional requirements while supporting the day-to-day administrative and operational functions of the Office of Financial Aid. The Financial Aid Operations Specialist serves as a primary point of contact for students and families and plays an important role in the overall management and coordination of office operations. The position works closely with Financial Aid staff, Student Accounts, and other campus partners to ensure effective service delivery, accurate processing, and a positive student experience. Position Responsibilities: Serve as a primary front-line resource for the Office of Financial Aid, responding to phone calls, emails, walk-in inquiries, and other requests from students and families. Provide information and guidance to students and families regarding financial aid programs, requirements, processes, deadlines, and available financing options. Perform quality assurance reviews of loans, awards, and other financial aid transactions to ensure accuracy and compliance with federal, state, and institutional regulations and procedures. Collaborate with Financial Aid Counselors to ensure student files are complete and external documentation requirements are satisfied, including entrance counseling, Master Promissory Notes (MPNs), verification requirements, and other required documentation. Process and maintain financial aid documents and records, ensuring information is accurately recorded, appropriately maintained, and routed for timely review and action. Manage alternative/private education loan processing, including certification and related administrative requirements. Perform loan certification and related loan-processing functions. Coordinate the processing and posting of outside scholarships in collaboration with Student Accounts, ensuring awards are accurately and timely reflected on student accounts and financial aid records. Gather, organize, and maintain information and documentation required for internal and external audits, compliance reviews, and other reporting needs. Assist with administrative responsibilities associated with former Perkins Loan borrowers and related records or inquiries. Manage and train Financial Aid student employees, including assigning work, providing guidance, and monitoring the quality and completion of assigned responsibilities. Serve as an office manager for the Office of Financial Aid, coordinating day-to-day administrative operations and helping ensure efficient office workflows, appropriate coverage, organization, and service delivery. Coordinate departmental administrative activities, including processing invoices, ordering and maintaining office supplies, and other office management responsibilities. Provide administrative support to the Director of Financial Aid, including coordination of departmental activities, projects, documentation, meetings, and other administrative needs. Serve as a project lead and/or departmental liaison for new College initiatives related to financial aid customer service, student experience, and operational improvements. Collaborate with Student Financial Services, Registrar, Admissions and other College departments to support coordinated student service and effective resolution of financial aid-related issues. Identify opportunities to improve administrative processes, customer service practices, and office workflows and assist with the implementation of operational improvements. Perform other responsibilities as assigned. Position Qualifications: Strong commitment to providing exceptional customer service, with demonstrated prior experience working directly with customers, students, families, or other constituents. Two or more years of financial aid experience in an administrative, operational, or counseling capacity within a higher education setting. Strong organizational, administrative, and problem-resolution skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Demonstrated ability to coordinate office operations, workflows, projects, and administrative processes. Good working knowledge of federal Title IV, Massachusetts state, and institutional financial aid regulations, policies, and procedures. Preferred experience with federal financial aid systems, including NSLDS, FAA Access, and COD. Preferred experience with PowerFAIDS. Strong attention to detail and demonstrated ability to maintain accurate records and perform quality assurance reviews. Ability to work collaboratively across departments and effectively coordinate activities involving multiple stakeholders. Excellent verbal and written communication skills. Ability to exercise sound judgment, maintain confidentiality, and appropriately handle sensitive student and financial information. Bachelor’s degree or equivalent combination of education and relevant work experience. Application Materials Should Include: Resume Cover letter stating motivation and interest in the position, citing experience relevant to the qualifications and including experience with, and commitment to, our Catholic Augustinian mission and our values. Work Location This is an on-campus position as employees are essential in order to provide a fully on-campus, residential college experience for our students and the community. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,100 undergraduate, 2,500 graduate students and 50 doctoral students from 48 states and 63 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business and the graduate school of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 38th in the Regional Universities North category in 2026. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Salary Range: $50,000.00 - $55,000.00 Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Request More Info Visit Campus Apply Now Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info Maintenance Requests MyMack Web Editor Login Find People & Places Contact Us Employee Directory Faculty Directory Map and Directions Quick Links Athletics Bookstore Consumer Information Employment Events Calendar Give Library Offices and Services Parking and Transportation Terms of Use Title IX Together We Rise Copyright © 2026 Merrimack College. All Rights Reserved. Search Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School