Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-Campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Apply Visit See Programs Employment Opportunities Senior Assistant Director of Transfer Admission & Enrollment Services Back to Employment Opportunities Senior Assistant Director of Transfer Admission & Enrollment Services Posted: May 7, 2026 Position Code: 729 Position Overview: Merrimack College, which is one of the fastest-growing educational institutions in the country and is located just minutes from Boston, Massachusetts, is seeking an energetic, highly motivated, and goal-driven professional to join the Office of Undergraduate Admission. Reporting to the Director of Transfer Admission & Enrollment Services, the Senior Assistant Director of Transfer Admission & Enrollment Services will share responsibility for meeting institutional enrollment goals and serve as an advisor to prospective students and their families, both transfer, off-cycle freshmen, and non-traditional students. They will serve as front-line contact for parents and students through the matriculation cycle to support successful enrollment and retention. The Senior. Assistant Director of Transfer Admission & Enrollment Services will be a generalist and a specialist in enrollment areas including admission, orientation, financial aid, transfer credits and curriculum, and billing. This person will also contribute to the development and implementation of recruitment plans for prospective transfer students. They will lead transfer credit evaluation and systems maintenance for new students in Merrimack’s undergraduate programs. They will provide exceptional customer services and build students’ and family members’ affinity to Merrimack. They will regularly staff outreach campaigns utilizing multiple communication channels to identify and navigate any barriers to enrollment and matriculation, present information sessions and participate in admission events. During peak recruitment season especially, the Sr. Assistant Director may be called upon to support the freshman recruitment team. Primary Responsibilities Serve on the Undergraduate Admission team responsible for application generation, decisions and yield for transfer students, off-cycle first-time freshmen, and non-traditional students; act as territory manager for Transfer and January/Spring and late Spring/Summer first-year applicants. Provide exceptional customer service by establishing channels of communication with prospective students to introduce them to and inform them of Merrimack College; facilitate their relationship with the institution throughout the admission process starting at the inquiry stage through their enrollment at the college. Develop and execute recruitment plan and budget for all transfer student recruitment events with a focus on primary, secondary and tertiary market community colleges and previous first-time freshmen applicants. Represent Merrimack College to prospective students and their families by attending off campus recruitment events, which include college fairs/tabling events and individual visits at community colleges, in addition to conducting on–campus transfer events for students, families, and transfer advisors. Counsel and advise prospective students, their families, transfer advisors and other community members about the transfer admission process, transfer credit options, course selection at non-Merrimack institutions and effectively communicate Merrimack’s value proposition. Work with advising center staff and faculty to coordinate new student advising meetings and course registration. Assist in the maintenance and quality control of student records, transfer policies and transfer credit records, manage day-to-day credit coordination in transfer equivalency systems, and transfer credit review process for transfer and first-year student in collaboration with the office of the registrar and faculty. Develop and maintain a network of transfer advisor contacts. Keep these contacts apprised of current news about the Merrimack community and develop pathways to Merrimack for their students. Participate and represent Merrimack College through meetings, presenting group information sessions and active participation in signature programming such as Open Houses, Admitted Student Days, Shadow Days, and Orientation. Understand and effectively communicate enrollment and college information. Maintain knowledge of multiple departments which include but are not limited to: Admission, Financial Aid, Student Accounts and Advising. Stay curious about and up to date on all things Merrimack. Build effective professional working relationships with people at all levels across the campus, who are involved in recruitment, enrollment and retention of new undergraduate students. Supervise, provide ongoing training and delegate daily responsibilities to graduate fellow(s). Skills & Qualifications: Bachelor’s degree required, master’s degree preferred Valid U.S. driving license required. 3-5 years of professional experience, preferably in recruitment, sales, or admission. Experience working with transfer students and their families. Professional and positive customer series, phone etiquette, and written communication Demonstrate excellent communication ability and problem-solving skills to explain, facilitate and improve upon Merrimack’s student services. Self-starter with a positive attitude, proactive mindset, and strong work ethic. Ability to use critical thinking skills and demonstrate professional judgement. Skilled at learning, organizing, researching and recalling a wide range of information while staying up to date with the enrollment and retention priorities. Strong time management skills, the ability to multitask and prioritize work and adhere to a strong sense of professionalism. A strong knowledge of office management responsibilities, systems and procedures. Willing to work in a metrics driven position Experience with MS Office, Google Suite, Slate CRM, Jenzabar, TES, and other Merrimack and enrollment systems. Willingness to work nights and weekends as needed at various times throughout the year. Application Materials Should Include: Resume or CV Cover letter stating motivation and interest in the position, citing experience relevant to the qualifications and including experience with, and commitment to, our Catholic Augustinian mission and our values. Work Location This is an on-campus position as employees are essential in order to provide a fully on-campus, residential college experience for our students and the community. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,100 undergraduate, 2,500 graduate students and 50 doctoral students from 48 states and 63 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business and the graduate school of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 38th in the Regional Universities North category in 2026. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Salary Range: $68,000 - $71,000 Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Request More Info Visit Campus Apply Now Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info Maintenance Requests MyMack Web Editor Login Find People & Places Contact Us Employee Directory Faculty Directory Map and Directions Quick Links Athletics Bookstore Consumer Information Employment Events Calendar Give Library Offices and Services Parking and Transportation Terms of Use Title IX Together We Rise Copyright © 2026 Merrimack College. All Rights Reserved. Search Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Admission Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid Student Accounts Student Life Student Life Our Campus Housing & Residence Life Dining Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education Student Involvement Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transpo