      "title": "Adjunct Lecturer, Computer and Data Sciences",
      "description": "Adjunct Lecturer, Computer and Data Sciences | Merrimack College Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid Student Accounts Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus Housing & Residence Life Dining Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education Student Involvement Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-Campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Apply Visit See Programs Employment Opportunities Adjunct Lecturer, Computer and Data Sciences Back to Employment Opportunities Adjunct Lecturer, Computer and Data Sciences Posted: October 16, 2026 Position Description: The Department of Computer and Data Sciences within the School of Engineering and Computational Sciences at Merrimack College seeks applicants for the position of Adjunct Lecturer for the Spring 2027 and Summer 2027 semesters. Instructors are needed for a variety of courses in computer science, data science, information technology, and cybersecurity programs, both graduate and undergraduate. Adjunct faculty are expected to teach 2 or 4 contact hours per week (depending on class and level) and hold regular office hours. Course offerings provide some flexibility, and the department will work with faculty to ensure as smooth of an experience as possible. Qualifications: M.S. or Ph.D. in Computer Science, Data Science, Information Technology, Cybersecurity, Mathematics, or a related field. Industry experience is a bonus, but not required. Excellent verbal/written communication skills. Application Materials Should Include: Resume or Curriculum Vitae (CV). This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Compensation Minimum: $5,000 per 4-credit course Minimum: $3,750 per lab section The actual pay offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as, but not limited to, candidate qualifications and prior experience, scope of responsibilities, internal equity, and market considerations. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,000 undergraduate and 1,900 graduate students from 46 states and 45 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused academic programs in science, engineering, business, nursing, health sciences, education, social sciences and humanities across undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business, and the Graduate School of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest-growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 37th in the Regional Universities North category in 2025. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Request More Info Visit Campus Apply Now Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info Maintenance Requests MyMack Web Editor Login Find People & Places Contact Us Employee Directory Faculty Directory Map and Directions Quick Links Athletics Bookstore Consumer Information Employment Events Calendar Give Library Offices and Services Parking and Transportation Terms of Use Title IX Together We Rise Copyright © 2026 Merrimack College. All Rights Reserved. Search Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate