    "https://www.merrimack.edu/employment_opportunities/assistant-director-senior-assistant-director-of-admission/": {
      "title": "Assistant Director / Senior Assistant Director of Admission",
      "description": "Assistant Director / Senior Assistant Director of Admission | Merrimack College Skip to content Students Faculty Staff Parents Alumni Give Together We Rise Academics Close Academics Open Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificates Online Programs Applied Bachelor's Degrees (3-Year) $17K Bachelor's Degree Programs Online Bachelor's Degree Programs Direct-Entry Master’s Programs Winter & Summer Sessions Research Experiential Learning Co-ops & Internships Study Abroad Service Learning Warriors at Work Learning Communities Austin Scholars Compass Honors Program Schools Girard School of Business School of Arts & Sciences School of Education & Social Policy School of Engineering & Computational Sciences School of Nursing & Health Sciences Graduate School of Counseling & Social Work Catalogs & Calendars Undergraduate Catalog Graduate Catalog Academic Calendar Student Success Academic Success Center O'Brien Center for Career Development The Lucey Center for Academic and Career Advising The Mack Force Office of the Provost Corporate Partnerships Admission Close Admission Open Admission Admission Apply Now! The Common App is now open— no app fee or test scores required. Undergraduate How to Apply Cost of Attendance Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid Transfer Admission International Students Undergraduate Events Graduate How to Apply Tuition and Fees Graduate Fellowships Scholarships & Grants Financial Aid International Students Graduate Events Professional & Continuing Studies Financial Aid Student Accounts Office of Institutional Effectiveness Student Life Close Student Life Open Student Life Student Life Our Campus Housing & Residence Life Dining Health & Wellness Campus Fitness Center & Recreation The Counseling Center Hamel Health Center Office of Wellness Education Student Involvement Clubs & Organizations Community Service Fraternity & Sorority Life Student Leadership Arts & Culture Student Union Athletics NCAA Division I Athletics Club Sports Intramural Sports On-Campus Services Bookstore Campus Safety McQuade Library Parking & Transportation Post Office Academic Support Academic Support & Advising International Student Support Graduate Center Student Financial Services & Registrar Financial Aid Registrar & Student Records Student Accounts The Mack Force Spiritual Life Grace J. Palmisano Center for Campus Ministry Service Learning About Close About Open About About Visit Merrimack Tour our beautiful New England campus and picture life as a Warrior. Our Story & Events About the College Mission History Strategic Plan Newsroom Calendar of Events Our Campus Our People Employee Directory Faculty Directory Human Resources Offices and Services College Leadership Office of the President Facts & Figures Accreditations Awards and Recognition Higher Education Opportunity Act (HEOA) Consumer Information Corporate Partnerships Maps & Directions Search Close Search Open Search Search Apply Visit See Programs Employment Opportunities Assistant Director / Senior Assistant Director of Admission Back to Employment Opportunities Assistant Director / Senior Assistant Director of Admission Posted: October 19, 2026 Position Code: 613 Position Overview: Merrimack College, which is one of the fastest-growing educational institutions in the country and is located just minutes from Boston, Massachusetts, is seeking an energetic, highly motivated, and goal-driven professional to join the Office of Undergraduate Admission as an Assistant/Senior Assistant Director of Admission. Reporting to the Associate Director, this role is responsible for driving undergraduate enrollment through strategic recruitment, relationship building, and data-informed outreach. The successful candidate will serve as a primary ambassador of the College, guiding prospective students and families through the admissions process while advancing institutional enrollment goals. Key responsibilities for the position: Enrollment & Territory Management Develop and execute a data-informed recruitment strategy for an assigned geographic territory Meet or exceed enrollment goals, including applications, admits, and deposits Analyze performance metrics and adjust outreach strategies to optimize results Student Engagement & Recruitment Build strong relationships with prospective students, families, school counselors, and community partners Deliver compelling, personalized communication across multiple channels (phone, email, text, in-person) Represent the College at high schools, college fairs, and recruitment events (8-12 weeks travel annually) Campus Presence & Events Serve as Counselor of the Day, conducting information sessions and advising visitors Support on-campus, virtual, and off-campus recruitment and yield events Provide a high level of customer service throughout the admissions experience Application Review & Operations Evaluate first-year applications and make admissions recommendations aligned with institutional policies Maintain accurate records and engagement tracking within the CRM system (Slate) Collaborate with campus partners to support enrollment initiatives Leadership & Collaboration (Senior Assistant Director) Supervise, mentor, and develop junior staff Lead key projects and initiatives within the admission office Serve as a liaison to campus stakeholders and contribute to strategic planning Qualifications and Skills Bachelor’s degree required, master’s degree preferred Valid U.S. driving license required. 1-2 years of experience (Assistant Director) or 2-4 years of experience (Senior Assistant Director) in admissions, recruitment, sales, or a related field. Demonstrated ability to manage a rigorous travel schedule, including extended periods of independent travel, while effectively representing the institution Adaptability in a fast-paced environment Strong multi-tasking, organization and time management skills Demonstrated ability to thrive in a data-oriented and analytical environment that has a high level of individual and team accountability Demonstrated ability to communicate clearly and effectively both verbally, and in writing Ability to establish and maintain effective relationships with prospective students, parents, school counselors, alumni, colleagues, and members of the Merrimack community Demonstrated ability to manage competing priorities, adapt quickly, and consistently deliver results in a fast-paced, goal-driven environment. Demonstrated ability to independently manage projects over time (Senior Assistant Director) Experience with MS Office, Google Suite, Slate CRM Willingness to work nights and weekends as needed at various times throughout the year. Application Materials Should Include: Resume or CV Cover letter stating motivation and interest in the position, citing experience relevant to the qualifications and including experience with, and commitment to, our Catholic Augustinian mission and our values. Work Location This is an on-campus position as employees are essential in order to provide a fully on-campus, residential college experience for our students and the community. This position is subject to the successful completion of a criminal background check. Statement on Our Mission Merrimack College is a Catholic Augustinian institution of higher education committed to building an accepting and respectful community. Our mission is to enlighten minds, engage hearts and empower lives and is inspired by our Catholic faith and the Augustinian tradition of seeking truth through inquiry and dialogue. Merrimack College seeks candidates who understand, respect, and can contribute to Merrimack’s Catholic and Augustinian mission. All candidates should describe in their application how they will foster a culture that supports our mission. About Merrimack College The only Catholic, Augustinian institution of higher education in New England, Merrimack College is a private, independent, coeducational institution with more than 4,100 undergraduate, 2,500 graduate students and 50 doctoral students from 48 states and 63 countries. The College features more than 160 career-focused undergraduate, professional and graduate programs, all taught by exceptional faculty who are passionate about their subject and student success. The College has six schools: arts and sciences, engineering and computational sciences, nursing and health sciences, education and social policy, the Girard school of business and the graduate school of counseling and social work. The College’s suburban 220-acre campus is just north of Boston in North Andover, Massachusetts. Merrimack is a Master’s Colleges and Universities/Larger Programs (M1) institution in the Carnegie Classification of Institutions of Higher Education. Merrimack is one of the fastest growing educational institutions in the country and has steadily climbed up in the U.S. News & World Report’s ranking of Best Colleges, ranking 38th in the Regional Universities North category in 2026. Merrimack is a NCAA Division I athletic institution. Merrimack College is an Equal Opportunity Employer. Salary Range: $60,000 - $70,000 Internal Applicants - Apply Now External Applicants - Apply Now Request More Info Visit Campus Apply Now Facebook-f Instagram Tiktok Youtube Linkedin-in X (formerly Twitter) Merrimack College 315 Turnpike Street North Andover, MA 01845 (978) 837-5000 Directions Internal Links Accessibility Canvas Catalog Email Emergency Info Maintenance Requests MyMack Web Editor Login Find People & Places Contact Us Employee Directory Faculty Directory Map and Directions Quick Links Athletics Bookstore Consumer Information Employment Events Calendar Give Library Offices and Services Parking and Transportation Terms of Use Title IX Together We Rise Copyright © 2026 Merrimack College. All Rights Reserved. Search Academics Academics Program Search Degrees & Majors Undergraduate Majors & Minors Graduate Degrees & Certificat